{"auditVerdictAtHead":"pass","canonicalDigest":"sha256:e4622a23afab6d9eb85bfa47d1610c7d435d9c2e468bc4d7e16ac8d7307e1ce2","canonicalizationVersion":"1","changeRequest":{"author":"buger","body":"Fixes #13250, fixes #13492, fixes #13493.\n\nThis replaces #13255, #13511 and #13512, which fixed these bugs one at a time and conflicted in `menu-test.sh`. It is two commits on `quattro` `8b4eae6`: the fix, and a follow-up for Unicode whitespace found in review.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Three menu-JSONC parsing bugs, fixed in one string-aware pass. The shipped menu parses unchanged (the same 344 rows), and the result is compared against #13681 on 200,000 generated documents.\n\n### What this changes\n\n| Issue | What goes wrong on `quattro` | After this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#13250** | a comma inside a string (`, ]` or `, }` in a label or action) is silently eaten | the string is kept intact |\n| **#13492** | an array root turns into entries `\"0\"`, `\"1\"`, … | an array root contributes no entries |\n| **#13493** | one inline `//` comment makes the whole file fail to parse | inline comments are handled, the file parses |\n| **Unicode whitespace, vertical tab, form feed** | a BOM, no-break space or other Unicode space, a vertical tab or a form feed works only right before a `//` comment (the comment regex's `\\s` swallows it); anywhere else the file fails to parse | read as plain whitespace anywhere outside a string |\n\n`stripJsonc` becomes one string-aware pass, and `parseMenuJsonc` returns no rows for an array root. The pass keeps what `quattro` got from `\\s` by accident: a file saved with a BOM and a leading `//` comment still parses, and now so does one without the comment. `docs/menu.md` states these rules.\n\n<details><summary>How the new pass works</summary>\n\nString contents are copied as is; outside a string, `//` drops the rest of its line (keeping the newline), a comma is dropped only when the next thing that isn't whitespace or a `//` comment is `}` or `]`, and any other whitespace character (JS `\\s`, which includes a BOM, the Unicode spaces, vertical tab and form feed) is passed on as a plain space. `parseMenuJsonc` returns no rows for an array root, as it already does for `null`, numbers and strings.\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Reproduce each bug (one-liners, from the repo root)</summary>\n\n**#13250 — commas inside strings are eaten.** The trailing-comma regex doesn't know about strings, so a `, ]` or `, }` inside a label or action gets \"repaired\" and the parse still succeeds:\n\n```sh\nnode -e 'const m=require(\"./shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js\"); console.log(m.parseMenuJsonc(`{\"b\": {\"label\": \"x, ]y\", \"action\": \"mv f{.bak,}\"}}`).map(r => [r.label, r.action]))'\n```\n\n`quattro`: `[ [ 'x ]y', 'mv f{.bak}' ] ]`. This PR: `[ [ 'x, ]y', 'mv f{.bak,}' ] ]`.\n\n**#13492 — an array root turns into entries `\"0\"`, `\"1\"`, ….** `typeof [] === \"object\"`, so an array passes the root check and `for..in` walks its indices:\n\n```sh\nnode -e 'const m=require(\"./shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js\"); console.log(m.parseMenuJsonc(`[{\"label\": \"x\"}, {\"label\": \"y\"}]`).map(r => r.id))'\n```\n\n`quattro`: `[ '0', '1' ]`. This PR: `[]`.\n\n**#13493 — one inline comment empties the menu.** Only whole-line `//` comments are stripped, so an inline tail reaches `JSON.parse`, which throws:\n\n```sh\nnode -e 'const m=require(\"./shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js\"); console.log(m.parseMenuJsonc(`{\"a\": {\"label\": \"A\"}} // note`).length)'\n```\n\n`quattro`: `0`. This PR: `1`.\n\n</details>\n\nA 21-second capture of the shipped parser on `quattro` `8b4eae6` and then on this branch's head `b2dae8db`, reading a menu whose last entry ends with a trailing comma and an inline `// favorites` comment, and the shipped sample config with its examples enabled: `quattro` returns 0 rows, this branch returns all 3:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1b4fc51-112c-4316-b5ac-7f744f7e6a62\n\n### What it could affect\n\nOnly `stripJsonc` and `parseMenuJsonc` in `shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js`; the shipped menu parses to the **same 344 rows, with identical row data**. `/* */` block comments stay unsupported.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> A trailing comma, then a `//` comment line, then `}` must keep parsing: the sample extension looks like that once its example rows are uncommented. #13512 and #13681 both break it; here the comma check also skips comments.\n\n<details><summary>Reproduce the trailing-comma-then-comment shape</summary>\n\nThe sample extension is `config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc`. Folding comments into the scanner breaks this shape unless the comma check also skips comments — which is why that clause is there.\n\n```sh\nnode -e 'const m=require(\"./shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js\"); console.log(m.parseMenuJsonc(`{\\n  \"a\": {\"label\": \"A\"},\\n  // \"b\": {\"label\": \"B\"},\\n}`).length)'\n```\n\n`quattro`: `1`. #13512 (`f75205f`) and #13681 (`6acbace`): `0`. This PR: `1`.\n\n</details>\n\n### How to check it\n\n- [x] `test/shell.d/menu-test.sh` gets **35 new assertions** (127 → 162 `ok`)\n- [x] every branch and condition in the rewritten parser is exercised in both directions\n- [x] the shipped menu is unchanged: 344 rows, identical row data\n- [x] every menu test still passes, and so do the related PRs' own `menu-test.sh` files\n- [x] 200,000 generated documents parse the same as #13681, except for the comma fix\n- [x] with all 19 non-ASCII whitespace characters inserted between tokens, before comments and at the start of the file, no generated document that `quattro` parses correctly parses differently here (the menu code is unchanged between `8b4eae6` and the current tip `c05d901`)\n\n<details><summary>The 35 new assertions — 15 that fail on <code>quattro</code>, 20 that pin behaviour it already gets right</summary>\n\n- **15 fail on `quattro`:** comma inside a label and inside an action; array root, plain and commented; inline tail; mixed whole-line and inline comments; JSON syntax inside a comment; trailing comma then an inline comment before `}` and before `]`; a BOM, no-break space, line separator, ideographic space, vertical tab or form feed before `{` with no comment.\n- **20 pin behaviour `quattro` already gets right:** escaped backslash before a trailing comma; object root; an `items` array skipped while its sibling entry still parses; `//` inside a string; trailing comma, whole-line comment, `}`; `{\"n\": 1//c` + newline + `2}` still rejected; the sample extension with its example rows uncommented; the same six characters before a leading `//` comment and indenting a `//` line (`quattro` handles these only through `\\s`, and the first commit here broke them); Unicode spaces inside a string kept as is.\n\nTogether with the generated-input comparison below, these exercise every branch and condition in the rewritten parser in both directions.\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Run every menu test, and the related PRs' own tests, against this branch</summary>\n\nEvery shell test that reads the menu parser or menu files passes on this branch, as on `quattro` (Linux, Node 26):\n\n```sh\nfor f in $(grep -rlE 'MenuModel|parseMenuJsonc|stripJsonc|omarchy-menu\\.jsonc|menu/Menu\\.qml' test/shell.d); do bash \"$f\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"ok   $f\" || echo \"FAIL $f\"; done\n```\n\nThe `menu-test.sh` files from #13255, #13511, #13512, #13681, #13305 and #6525 also pass when run against this branch's code.\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Compare with #13681 on 200,000 generated documents (<code>compare.js</code>)</summary>\n\nSave the script below as `compare.js` and run:\n\n```sh\ngit fetch https://github.com/omacom/omarchy pull/13681/head && git show FETCH_HEAD:shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js > /tmp/MenuModel-13681.js && node compare.js /tmp/MenuModel-13681.js\n```\n\nIt prints `200000 documents: 4187 parse differently; with the comment-skip clause off: 0`. So on this input the comma check is the only difference in stripping.\n\n```js\n// node compare.js <other MenuModel.js>   (from the repo root of this branch)\n// Generates JSONC documents and compares what this branch's stripJsonc and the\n// other file's stripJsonc parse them to. Also reruns the comparison with this\n// branch's \"skip // comments after a comma\" clause turned off.\nconst fs = require('fs'), vm = require('vm')\nconst load = src => { const c = {}; vm.runInNewContext(src + '\\nthis.s = stripJsonc', c); return c.s }\nconst mine = fs.readFileSync('shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js', 'utf8')\nconst noSkip = mine.replace(/\\} else if \\(input\\[next\\] === \"\\/\" && input\\[next \\+ 1\\] === \"\\/\"\\) \\{/, '} else if (false) {')\nif (noSkip === mine) throw new Error('comment-skip clause not found')\nconst a = load(mine), b = load(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[2], 'utf8')), c = load(noSkip)\nlet seed = 7\nconst rnd = n => (seed = (seed * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7fffffff) % n, pick = xs => xs[rnd(xs.length)]\nconst ws = () => pick(['', ' ', '\\n', '  ', '\\r\\n', '\\t', ' \\f', ' '])\nconst com = () => pick(['', '', '// c\\n', '// \"q\" , ] }\\n', ' // x', '//\\n', ' // t\\n'])\nconst str = () => '\"' + pick(['x', 'x, ]y', 'a // b', 'q\\\\\\\\', 'e\\\\\"', '{.bak,}', 'u']) + '\"'\nconst val = d => [str, () => pick(['1', 'true', 'null']), () => arr(d + 1), () => obj(d + 1)][rnd(d > 2 ? 2 : 4)]()\nconst list = (o, c, item) => { let n = rnd(3), s = o + ws() + com(); for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { s += item() + ws() + com(); if (i < n - 1 || rnd(2)) s += ',' + ws() + com() } return s + ws() + c }\nconst arr = d => list('[', ']', () => val(d))\nconst obj = d => list('{', '}', () => pick(['\"a\"', '\"label\"', '\"action\"', '\"aliases\"']) + ws() + ':' + ws() + val(d))\nconst parse = (f, s) => { try { return JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(f(s))) } catch (e) { return 'ERR' } }\nconst N = 200000\nlet differ = 0, differNoSkip = 0\nfor (let k = 0; k < N; k++) {\n  const s = com() + (rnd(5) ? obj(0) : arr(0)) + ws() + com()\n  const pb = parse(b, s)\n  if (parse(a, s) !== pb) differ++\n  if (parse(c, s) !== pb) differNoSkip++\n}\nconsole.log(`${N} documents: ${differ} parse differently; with the comment-skip clause off: ${differNoSkip}`)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Open points\n\n#13681 by @AnPod fixes the same three issues the same way, except for the comma check and the whitespace handling above: on #13681, a BOM, no-break space, vertical tab or form feed before a `//` comment empties the file, as it did on this PR's first commit. #13305 and #6525 touch the same lines, so whichever lands first makes the others conflict.\n\n<details><summary>Related PRs</summary>\n\n| PR | What it covers | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| #13681 by @AnPod | the same three issues, same approach | apart from the comma check and whitespace handling above, it behaves the same; it also rejects array roots |\n| #13305 by @Cid-oe | #13250 on its own | touches the same lines |\n| #6525 by @itscallssh | inline comments | touches the same lines |\n\n</details>\n\n### What I'm asking\n\nA review of this as the single fix for #13250, #13492 and #13493.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> If you'd rather merge #13681, carrying over the comma lookahead, the whitespace branch and their tests would be enough, and I'll close this one.\n\n---\n\n**Independent verification:** the menu parser's requirements, tests and coverage are on <https://portal.reqproof.com/projects/omarchy>.\n\n---\n\n**Updated 2026-10-01:** Added `b2dae8d`: a BOM or other Unicode space before a `//` comment parsed on `quattro` only because the old regex's `\\s` swallowed it, and the first commit broke that (thanks, Greptile). Whitespace outside strings (including a vertical tab or form feed, which `\\s` also matches) is now read as a space, so it also parses without a comment; 19 new assertions. Also 2026-10-02: re-recorded the capture on the head `b2dae8d`; in the old one the `0 rows` result was hidden under a caption.\n","bodyDigest":"sha256:7fa6367e4c6d4f9c1844c2e12623e3b58d537da5bdc98e0f60067469587df296","bodyExcerpt":"Fixes #13250, fixes #13492, fixes #13493.","linkedIssues":["#13250","#13492","#13493"],"source":"explicit","title":"Fix menu JSONC parsing: commas in strings, array roots, inline comments"},"createdAt":"2026-10-01T23:32:33Z","decisionSummary":{"claimEvidence":[{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-2JZT","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"passed":0,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","status":"not_linked","tests":0},{"class":"external_call_timeout_bounded","failed":0,"passed":0,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","status":"not_linked","tests":0}],"passed":2,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-2JZT","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_changed_as_intended","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","failed":0,"passed":2,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":2},{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"passed":2,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":2},{"class":"input_domain","failed":0,"passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":1}],"passed":3,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-46HY","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","failed":0,"observedVia":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","status":"observed_pass","tests":1},{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"observedVia":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","status":"observed_pass","tests":1}],"passed":3,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-46HY","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-74BZ","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","fail